    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Increase losartan to 100 mg daily today and continue amlodipine 10 mg daily. [S]</item><item>Start dapagliflozin 10 mg daily today: eGFR is above 20 and albuminuria above 200 mg/g. It is for kidney protection, so continue it even if eGFR later falls below 20. [S]</item><item>Accept a creatinine rise of up to 30 percent from 2.1 mg/dL after these changes; check potassium and creatinine in about three weeks. [S]</item><item>If blood pressure is still above target on full doses of losartan and amlodipine, add chlorthalidone 12.5 mg daily, which works at his level of kidney function. [S]</item><item>Target a standardized office systolic pressure below 120 mmHg if tolerated, with below 130/80 as the first step. [S]</item><item>Avoid NSAIDs; sick-day rule to hold losartan, dapagliflozin, and any diuretic on days with vomiting, diarrhea, or poor fluid intake. [S]</item><item>Sodium below 2 g a day, with a plan for meals while traveling. [S]</item><item>Urine albumin-creatinine ratio once the regimen is complete. Urinalysis with microscopy and further testing for other kidney diseases if albuminuria does not fall on treatment or kidney function changes unexpectedly. [S]</item><item>Calcium, phosphate, PTH, and a baseline 25-hydroxyvitamin D at about six months; hemoglobin at least yearly. No alkali, vitamin D analog, or iron now. [S]</item><item>Pneumococcal and hepatitis B vaccination for chronic kidney disease. [S]</item><item>Calculate the kidney failure risk once eGFR has settled on full therapy. [S]</item><item>Discussed with Dr. Whitfield in person today; the patient agrees with the plan. [S]</item><item>Follow-up: Primary care will manage titration and monitoring on the CMID schedule, with eGFR and urine albumin about three times a year. Nephrology will review him with the six-month results and the kidney failure risk, and sooner for a creatinine rise of more than 30 percent, potassium above 5.5 mmol/L, blood pressure above target on three agents, or albuminuria that does not fall. [S]</item></list></text>

